 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Not at all. Many restaurants give you few minutes to finish before they start cleaning. Asking right away helps us get your check right away. That's easy. Just divide by two and round up. Each person pays a bit more, but everyone contributes. I'd lean towards tipping each waiter as if they' served few people instead of per person. It distributes the load more fairly. You' welcome. Eating out with friends is great, and little bits of politeness make it much nicer for everyone.",
